          "nudge_reason": null,
          "final_text_tail": " context was never closed (no `__exit__`/`close()`), the file handle was never released \u2192 `ResourceWarning: unclosed file`.\n\n**Fix** (`src/click/shell_completion.py`, `_resolve_context`): Wrapped all three context creation calls in `with` statements so each context's `__exit__` \u2192 `close()` runs, executing the `call_on_close` callbacks that close file handles:\n1. Main: `with cli.make_context(...) as ctx:`\n2. Non-chained group sub-context: `with cmd.make_context(...) as sub_ctx:`\n3. Chained group sub-context: `with cmd.make_context(...) as sub_sub_ctx:`\n\nThe function still returns the (now-closed) context, which remains fully usable by `shell_complete` \u2014 closing only resets the exit stack, leaving `params`/`command`/`args`/`parent` intact.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Before fix: 5/6 scenarios leaked a `ResourceWarning`.\n- After fix: all 6 scenarios (command file option, group file option, subcommand file option, chained file option, chained multiple, file argument) show **0** ResourceWarnings.\n- Full test suite: **614 passed**, 21 skipped, 1 xfailed \u2014 no regressions. (The only collection error, a `PytestRemovedIn10Warning` in `test_basic.py`, is pre-existing and unrelated to this change.)\n\n**Note on `core.py`:** The task's \"Files Modified\" list includes `src/click/core.py`, but the described \"Solution\" covers only the `shell_completion.py` `with`-statement changes, which I implemented exactly. No `core.py` change is required \u2014 the leak is fully resolved and all tests pass without one.",
